# kant over the corpus's shared atoms, written by phil/corpus from readings/kant/logic: not to be edited
atom	universal	my maxim is a universal law: everyone in difficulty may promise whatever he pleases with the purpose of not keeping it
atom	nobody_believes	no one would consider that anything was promised to him, but would ridicule all such statements as vain pretences
atom	promise_possible	the promise itself, and the end one has in view in it, is possible
atom	holds	the maxim holds as a universal law of nature without contradicting itself
P1	S8	universal → nobody_believes
P2	S8	nobody_believes → ¬promise_possible
C1	S8	universal → ¬promise_possible	from P1 P2
A1	-	holds → universal ∧ promise_possible	kind conceptual
C	S7	¬holds	from C1 A1
